      "content": "thanks for this, it's a good start. i noticed the score for that draft was only around 13, which is kind of low. honestly, my supervisor is really stickler for seeing the full breadth of the field. \n\ncould you expand this into a much more detailed summary? try to weave in as many of those names from the list as humanly possible so the score is closer to the max. i don't care if the paragraphs get a bit long, just make sure every major researcher is mentioned so the coverage score is high. it's really important that the tool flags this as a \"highly comprehensive\" review.",
